// An empty path names no directory, in both forms of mkdir
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, mkdir): the call raises the catchable DirectoryError,
// so a program can report it and go on.
// A consumer that resolves the empty path to the working directory, as the
// JDK does, creates something and raises nothing.
// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: DirectoryError
// CHECK: DirectoryError
try { mkdir(""); } catch (e) { print e.kind; }
try { mkdir("", "p"); } catch (e) { print e.kind; }
